course: dictionary
lesson: 2994
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word dump is a good example. To find the right meaning, read the words around it: they are its context. «He dumped his heavy bag on the floor» means he dropped it roughly, because of the word floor and the way he let it fall.
explain: «They took the old sofa to the dump.» Here dump means a place where rubbish is taken and left. Ask yourself: does my meaning fit the sentence? You can test it by swapping in your meaning and checking that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Some meanings are informal, which means you would use them in chatty speech, not in school writing. «Ravi is down in the dumps» means he is sad. «This place is a dump!» means it is dirty, messy or ugly. Look at the whole sentence and the feeling in it to be sure which meaning the writer means.
fact: Dump can be a verb (an action) or a noun (a thing or a place).
fact: To dump something means to put it down carelessly or roughly, or to get rid of rubbish in a place where it is not allowed.
fact: A dump, or tip in the UK and Australia, is a place where rubbish is taken and left.
fact: «Down in the dumps» means sad.
fact: «This place is a dump!» is informal and means dirty, messy or ugly.
exercise: «He dumped his heavy bag on the floor and sat down.» What does dumped mean here? | Carefully lifted up high | Filled with water | Hidden under the bed | *Put down roughly, letting it fall
exercise: «They took the old sofa to the dump.» What is the dump? | A bicycle shed | A type of cake | *A place where rubbish is taken and left | A big, cosy bed
exercise: «Ravi felt down in the dumps after losing the match.» What does down in the dumps mean? | Dirty from playing in the mud | Hiding in a cave | Very excited | *Sad
test: «Dumping rubbish in the park is against the rules and harms nature.» What does dumping rubbish mean here? | Carefully sorting it into bins | *Getting rid of it in a place where it is not allowed | Cleaning up the park | Taking a photo of it
test: Gerry says the caravan is a dump. What does he mean? | *It is dirty, messy or ugly | It is made of wood | It has just been painted | It is a real rubbish dump
exam: «Some storks now eat at rubbish dumps instead of flying to Africa.» What is a rubbish dump? | A bird that flies to Africa | A kind of food | *A place where rubbish is taken and left | A nest high in a tree
